{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'categor.*domain|domain.*categor|categor.*zoom' docs packages/axylo/src packages/axylo/test | head -75; sed -n '216,244p' packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts; sed -n '154,186p' packages/axylo/src/diagnostics/registry.ts\"","aggregated_output":"docs/02-product-spec.md:111:| L1 | No visible text overlaps other text or is clipped, and no label disappears without the reader being told. Remedies, in order: thin (time, date, numeric and `ordered` category axes only); wrap to two lines; rotate up to 45°; truncate in the middle, keeping every label distinct, with the full text in tooltip and table. If labels still do not fit, a visible note (\"Some labels hidden. See table.\") appears and AX143 suggests horizontal bars. Axylo never changes a chart's orientation on its own. | In real browsers, after fonts load: for widths 240–1,920 px and generated label sets, zero intersecting text boxes (1 px tolerance), zero text outside the figure, truncated labels pairwise distinct. Repeated with the WCAG 1.4.12 text-spacing overrides, 200% text-only zoom, and a font that loads late | R2 |\npackages/axylo/src/view/index.ts:185:  const author = category ? null : readSpan(authorInput, readX, 'x.domain', sink);\npackages/axylo/src/view/index.ts:189:  const zoom = compact || category && state.kind === 'bar' ? null : readSpan(state.zoom, readX, 'zoom', sink);\npackages/axylo/src/core/axes.ts:64:  kind: Exclude<XKind, 'category'>, domain: Span, timeZone: string | null, dateUnit: 'day' | 'month' | 'year' | null,\npackages/axylo/src/core/axes.ts:134: * size, text style, fonts, locale, domains, categories, titles and formatters.\npackages/axylo/src/core/contracts.ts:219:  /** Position in the scale's domain (category: index). */\n    zoom: Span<XValue> | null;\n    follow: boolean;\n  }\n\n  function buildViewFor(draft: Draft, previous: Accepted | null): Pick<Accepted, 'view' | 'viewKey' | 'viewDiagnostics'> {\n    const key = viewKeyFor(draft.options, draft.resolved, draft.frame, draft.zoom);\n    if (previous && sameValue(previous.viewKey, key)) {\n      return { view: previous.view, viewKey: previous.viewKey, viewDiagnostics: previous.viewDiagnostics };\n    }\n    stage('view');\n    const sink = new DiagnosticCollector();\n    const view = buildView(draft.frame as never, viewStateFor(draft.options, draft.resolved, draft.zoom, previous?.view ?? null) as never, sink) as View;\n    const viewDiagnostics = sink.inputs();\n    draft.found.push(...viewDiagnostics);\n    return { view, viewKey: key, viewDiagnostics };\n  }\n\n  function namingDiagnostics(options: OptionRecord): DiagnosticInput[] {\n    if (titleOf(options) !== null || stringOption(options, 'labelledBy') !== null) return [];\n    const sink = new DiagnosticCollector();\n    report(sink, 'AX140', 'none');\n    return [...sink.inputs()];\n  }\n\n  function normalizeInto(draft: Draft): void {\n    stage('normalize');\n    const sink = new DiagnosticCollector();\n    const version = { epoch: draft.epoch, revision: (accepted?.frame.revision ?? 0) + 1 };\n    if (kind === 'line' || kind === 'area' || kind === 'bar') {\n}\n\nexport function createDiagnostic(\n  code: DiagnosticCode,\n  effect: DiagnosticEffect,\n  details: DiagnosticDetails = {},\n  origin: DiagnosticInput['origin'] = 'call',\n): DiagnosticInput {\n  const { field, rows, count = rows?.length, ...context } = details;\n  const firstRows = rows === undefined ? undefined : [...new Set(rows)].slice(0, 10);\n  const outcome = context.outcome ?? (\n    code === 'AX102' && effect === 'changed' ? 'Shown as zeros.'\n      : code === 'AX108' && effect === 'chart-error' ? 'The donut is not drawn.'\n      : code === 'AX150' && effect === 'chart-error' ? 'The chart shows its error state.'\n      : undefined\n  );\n  const diagnostic: DiagnosticInput = {\n    code, level: diagnosticRegistry[code].level, effect: code === 'AX105' ? 'none' : effect, origin,\n    message: diagnosticRegistry[code].message({ field, rows: firstRows, count, ...context, outcome }),\n    ...(field === undefined ? {} : { field }),\n    ...(firstRows === undefined ? {} : { rows: firstRows }),\n    ...(count === undefined ? {} : { count }),\n  };\n  contexts.set(diagnostic, context);\n  return diagnostic;\n}\n\nexport function report(sink: DiagnosticSink, code: DiagnosticCode, effect: DiagnosticEffect, details?: DiagnosticDetails): void {\n  sink.add(createDiagnostic(code, effect, details));\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
